    "end": "Spring by the sausage rolls.",
    "caption": "Blink and you'll miss the warm bit.\n\nThaw: 720,000 people, a 29-hour day, two moons, and a climate that runs entirely on small talk. Every gathering here starts in deep winter: weddings, barbecues, the office do. Hosts lay on blankets and hot drinks, and wait. Everyone has a friend like Meera, who can thaw a room with one question about the dog. She is invited to absolutely everything.\n\nI tried 'Lovely weather.' Six inches, overnight.\n\n(The story goes that 'breaking the ice' first meant clearing a frozen river so the boats could get through. By the 1600s, it meant getting strangers talking.)\n\nWhat's your line for breaking the ice?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Kev's next party is in June. Meera has been asked to come early.",
